Same matgen, transpose and dot products in the same accumulation order. The reference uses Vec<Vec<f64>> (a row per allocation) and allocates the transpose and the product each run; here each matrix is one flat array indexed i * n + j and the arrays live in the state. The checksum hashes the formatted center element of every run: the center is identical each run, so the port answers it and the harness hashes it exactly as the reference helper does. Scratch state rebuilt every run (the reference's locals: bt, c) is not logged (state is unlogged by default, so no undo log, as a Rust local has none).
